# Bare PLURAL definite article marking habitual weekday recurrence -- "los
# lunes" / "las" (feminine agreement is never needed for a weekday noun, but
# both forms are listed for symmetry with the article vocabulary). RAE/DPD
# s.v. "el" -- the plural article on a day-of-the-week noun reads
# habitually ("Los lunes vamos al cine" -- "We go to the cinema on
# Mondays"), while the singular ("El lunes vamos al cine") names the single
# next Monday. Deliberately holds ONLY the plural surfaces: "el"/"la" are
# excluded so the singular reading is structurally unreachable here, not
# merely guarded against.
los
las
